  "text": "You realize just how amazing humans are, just how amazing your four-year-old is who can recognize faces. Machine learning has really been the beginning of a big revolution in the field of speech recognition. To teach speech recognition, how to interact with a noisy room. We use real-world sounds and we mix it into the examples that we already have. Is it cold outside? Now, no matter what the noise in the environment, our speech recognition systems can understand what you're saying. They can separate out one speaker from another. With machine learning, we have now an algorithm that learns how to simulate a human linguist. A lot of the language that we see today, it's very informal.",
